## RULES

- **Style.** Structure over prose in every design note, comment, and doc: headers,
  bullets, one idea per line. No throat-clearing. Cut a sentence if its removal loses no
  information. File:line citations over adjectives.
- **Quality bar** — %%reviewer_name%% judges against this, not the literal AC: %%quality_bar%%
- **Reuse before you write.** Grep for what already does it, read %%architecture_doc%%,
  check shared/utility dirs. Duplicating an existing helper is a review-blocking defect.
- **Right layer, real cause.** A workaround on the wrong layer needs a written reason
  and a follow-up task.
- **Tests are part of the change.** At the level that exercises the behavior; write the
  test first where the code allows. Never weaken/delete an assertion to get green.
- **Small, reviewable.** One task → one branch → one PR, `Ref #<n>` (never
  `Closes`/`Fixes`). Commits are coherent steps, not a dump.
- **Subagents** (`Agent`): `architect` reviews your design note before code — mandatory
  for `Size: M`/`L` or anything touching the data model/a shared module/a new
  dependency. `reviewer` reviews your diff — mandatory every task, two rounds max.
  Neither writes code.
- **Human override**: a `human:` comment newer than your last action wins. Only
  %%human_name%% can provide (credentials, infra, a product decision) → comment what
  you need, swap `in-progress` for `human-blocker`, move on.

